    "bounding box" : [ 81.6, 567.619, 428.658, 620.385 ],
    "font" : "CMR9",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Bona and Tzvetkov [1] proved that the BBM equation is globally well - posed in Hs(R) for s ≥ 0. The same result also holds for the periodic case [2, 3]. This well posedness is optimal, since if s < 0, the equation (1) is ill - posed in Hs(R). In fact, Bona and Tzvetkov [1] also proved that for s < 0, the solution map u0  → u(t) of the equation (1) is not a C2 map from Hs(R) to C([0, T]; Hs(R))."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 2,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 81.601, 539.31, 428.618, 565.665 ],
    "font" : "CMR9",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Later, Panthee [4] improved this result by showing that the solution map is not continuous from Hs(R) to D′(R) for any ﬁxed t > 0 small enough."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 3,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 95.4, 534.739, 405.671, 543.705 ],
    "font" : "CMR9",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Carvajal and Panthee [5] considered the following generalized BBM equation"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 4,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 194.761, 500.206, 312.396, 524.063 ],
    "font" : "CMR9",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "ut + ux + Lut + (uk+1)x = 0, u(0, x) = u0(x),"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "level" : "1",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 416.881, 507.378, 428.618, 516.345 ],
    "font" : "CMR9",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "(2)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 81.601, 471.39, 404.315, 488.183 ],
    "font" : "CMR9",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where L is deﬁned via the Fourier transform as Lu(ξ) = |ξ|α+1 ω(ξ), with α > 0."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 81.6, 421.819, 428.618, 477.263 ],
    "font" : "CMR9",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Carvajal and Panthee [5] proved that the equation (2) is locally well - posed in Hs(R) for some s depending on α and k. Moreover, if s < max{0, 21 − αk }, the equation (2) is ill - posed in Hs(R), which means that the solution map is not Ck+1 - diﬀerentiable from Hs(R) to C([0, T];Hs(R)) for any T > 0. When α = 1, some global well - posedness results for (2) with periodic boundary conditions were obtained [3]."
  }, {
